Use the vertical line test.
Is this graph a function?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->] (-2,-2.4)--(2,2.4);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the vertical line test.
Is this graph a function?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->,domain=-1.7:1.7,smooth,samples=60,variable=\y] plot ({2-\y*\y},{\y});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the vertical line test.
Is this graph a function?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->,domain=-1.9:1.9,smooth,samples=60,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.6*\x*\x-1});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

This circle is not a function.
Which pair of points on it shows that it fails the vertical line test?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (2);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the vertical line test.
Is this graph a function?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] (-2.6,1.6)--(-0.5,-1);
\draw[thick] (-0.5,1)--(2.6,1.9);
\draw[fill=white,thick] (-0.5,-1) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (-0.5,1) circle (2.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the vertical line test.
Is this graph a function?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,<->] (-2,-2.6)--(-2,2.6);
\node[below right,font=\scriptsize] at (-2,0) {$-2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the vertical line test.
Is this graph a function?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] (-2,0) arc (180:360:2);
\fill (-2,0) circle (2pt);
\fill (2,0) circle (2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
